---
title: Shrimp scampi
servings: 4
tags: [italian, seafood, weeknight]
cuisine: italian
time: 45 minutes
source: Shrimp Scampi with Pasta by Jennifer Segal, Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/shrimp-scampi.html
---

Bring a #large pot{} of well-salted water to a boil and cook the
@dried pasta{16%oz}(linguine, spaghetti, angel hair or fettuccine) until al
dente. Save 1 cup of the cooking water, then drain.

Meanwhile, heat the @extra virgin olive oil{1/3%cup} in a large #skillet{}
over medium heat. Cook the @shallots{3/4%cup}(thinly sliced, 2 to 3) ~{1%minute},
stirring.

Add the @garlic{6%cloves}(large, minced), @red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp},
@shrimp{1 1/4%lb}(extra-large, 26 to 30 per lb, peeled and deveined), and
1/4 tsp each of @salt{} and @black pepper{}. Cook ~{3%minutes}, stirring now
and then, until the shrimp are pink and only just done. Move them to a plate.

Pour the @dry white wine{3/4%cup} into the pan and simmer ~{3%minutes} to
~{4%minutes}, until it is reduced by half.

Add the @unsalted butter{6%tbsp}(in 4 pieces), @lemon juice{3%tbsp},
@lemon zest{1%tsp}, 1/2 cup of the pasta water and @salt{1/2%tsp}. Stir until
the butter melts.

Toss in the pasta until hot, loosening with more pasta water if it looks dry.
Return the shrimp and their juices, add the @parsley{1/4%cup}(finely chopped),
and toss again. Taste, adjust, and serve with @lemon{}(wedges).

> Take the shrimp off early: they finish cooking when they go back in with the pasta.
